{# 0300_ne_plot_awareness.prompt — the plot this NPC is part of, if any.

   SkyrimNet assembles every `.prompt` under
   `prompts/submodules/user_final_instructions/` into the closing
   instructions of the prompt, in numeric order. 0300 puts this after the
   combat status (0200) and ahead of the response format (0500), so it is
   read as part of the situation rather than as a rule about the reply.

   `ne_plot_awareness` is registered by NarrativeEngine's SKSE plugin (see
   Decorators.cpp and PlotAwareness.cpp). It answers with a record, as JSON
   that SkyrimNet parses into an object: a mastermind's scheme and each step
   of it, or an agent's errand. components/narrative_engine/plot_awareness
   .prompt words it in the second person. For anybody in no plot it answers
   empty, and this renders nothing. Custom decorators bind as
   `(uuid) -> string`, so it is called with `npc.UUID`.

   The closing line is the template's rather than the decorator's because
   it is the same for both roles: without it, a mastermind asked "are you
   plotting anything?" told the player the whole scheme. #}
{% if exists("npc") and existsIn(npc, "UUID") and not is_player(npc.UUID) %}
{% set plot_awareness = ne_plot_awareness(npc.UUID) %}
{% if plot_awareness != "" %}
## Your Plot

{% include "components/narrative_engine/plot_awareness.prompt" %}

This is a secret. You only discuss it with people you trust, or with those already involved in it.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
